Currently playing a human priest and doing really well.  The RNG loves
me this game.  I found an amulet of ESP in the first room and the next
level down I found speed boots and an oilskin sack.

Then in Sobakan I got a WoW (0:2)!  Got MR, SDSM, recharged with a
scroll from a shop.  Then wished up the Healer staff, a spell book of
identify, and a helm of brilliance.  Then I remembered the priest quest
item IS a helm  of brilliance!  Doh!

So I cruise through the dungeon ID'ing everything and finding lots of
good stuff.  I bypass the quest for now and clear out Medusa, the
Castle, Valley of the Dead and I just paid off Asmodeus.

But I got to say, when I got the second WoW from the Castle, I didn't
really know what to wish for.  I already had everything I wanted.  I
ended up getting a spellbook of remove curse, spellbook of magic
mapping (ok I wanted that, can't do Hell without it), 2 scrolls of
genocide, and then used 3 wishes trying to get the Wizard amulet.  No
luck though.  I've already seen the healer staff, magicbane, Trollbane,
and Cleaver, so the artifact counter is pretty high.  I haven't even
made Orcrist or Sting for points yet.

Anyway, my point is I started to get bored with the character.  Nothing
was challenging me, not even demons and undead who are level drain
resistant.  And when I get bored I tend to kill off my character and
make a new one.  Starting characters are more fun!

But I will probably ascend this priest (my 10th overall) and then my
next character will be wishless.  And genocideless.  I get excited when
I see Arch-Liches and Master Mind Flayers because I know they  can be
BIG trouble.



